Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: service REO status before RX exhausts NAPI

REO status, RX exceptions and WBM RX release share an interrupt group
on IPQ5332 and QCN6432 (and other Wi-Fi 7 variants). A saturated error
ring can consume every NAPI packet budget before the status ring is
visited. Command retirement then depends on RX becoming idle.

Visit REO status before packet work on positive-budget polls, preserving
the entire RX budget and TX completion behavior. The status reader drains
only the finite cached head-pointer snapshot, not an unbounded live ring.
Do not add status processing to zero-budget TX-only polls.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp.c
@@ -38,3 +38,9 @@
+	/* REO command completion must not depend on the RX packet budget.
+	 * Drain the finite status snapshot before RX errors can exhaust it.
+	 */
+	if (budget > 0 && dp->hw_params->ring_mask->reo_status[grp_id])
+		ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_process_reo_status(dp);
+
 	if (dp->hw_params->ring_mask->rx_err[grp_id]) {
 		work_done = ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_process_err(dp, napi, budget);
 		budget -= work_done;
@@ -124,9 +130,6 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}
-
-	if (dp->hw_params->ring_mask->reo_status[grp_id])
-		ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_process_reo_status(dp);
 
 	if (dp->hw_params->ring_mask->host2rxdma[grp_id]) {
 		struct dp_rxdma_ring *rx_ring = &dp->rx_refill_buf_ring;
